los contratos [1], [2], [3] atienden la misma necesidad. Verificar si el adjudicatario A repite contratos en otros ámbitos. Analizar si los contratos al límite coinciden con presupuestos cerrados o con necesidades distintas.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 32 minor contracts for services and supplies above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 5.0 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 6.4, with a 95% confidence interval of 3.7 to 11.3. December accounts for 34% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 25% of all its services and supplies contracts. The awardee with the most contracts just under the limit, called awardee A here, has 4. Contract [1], for 14,860 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The concentration of contracts in December does not indicate improper activity. Similar patterns can occur due to seasonal demand or budget cycles. Small amounts near the limit do not prove violations, as market prices or fixed budgets may influence spending.\nWhat can be checked: Check the dates and values of contracts to see if they align with seasonal trends. Review awardee A’s contracts to identify if multiple contracts serve the same purpose. Examine if contracts were awarded in December to meet annual budget deadlines.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["I7%2BqQ1VK%2BfeTylGzYmBF9Q%3D%3D","X0HBf81G%2Fow3vLk2DU2Ddg%3D%3D","a1s%2BBDdyjEZeKgd8LfVV9g%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}